<article class="env-lemma" id="03D4">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03D4">Lemma <span data-tag="03D4">18.12.4</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$, $\mathcal{D}$ be sites. Let $f : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D})$ be a morphism of topoi. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a sheaf of rings on $\mathcal{C}$. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a sheaf of $\mathcal{O}$-modules. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a sheaf of $f_*\mathcal{O}$-modules. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O})}( \mathcal{O} \otimes _{f^{-1}f_*\mathcal{O}} f^{-1}\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}) = \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{Mod}(f_*\mathcal{O})}(\mathcal{G}, f_*\mathcal{F}).  \]
</div>
  <p> Here we use Lemmas <a href="/tag/03D2" data-tag="03D2">18.12.2</a> and <a href="/tag/03D1" data-tag="03D1">18.12.1</a>, and we use the canonical map $f^{-1}f_*\mathcal{O} \to \mathcal{O}$ in the definition of the tensor product. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Note that we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{Mod}(\mathcal{O})}( \mathcal{O} \otimes _{f^{-1}f_*\mathcal{O}} f^{-1}\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}) = \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _{\textit{Mod}(f^{-1}f_*\mathcal{O})}( f^{-1}\mathcal{G}, \mathcal{F}_{f^{-1}f_*\mathcal{O}})  \]
</div>
    <p>
       by Lemma <a href="/tag/03CZ" data-tag="03CZ">18.11.3</a>. Hence the result follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/03D3" data-tag="03D3">18.12.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>